import json

_DATA = json.loads("[{\"fn\": \"fitout-shop-drawings/index.html\", \"title\": \"Fit-Out &amp; Joinery Shop Drawings UAE | D3DDD\", \"desc\": \"Fit-out and joinery shop drawings for UAE interiors: ceilings, partitions, kitchens, wardrobes and interior elevations, issued as DWG and PDF.\", \"body\": \"<section class=\\\"page-hero\\\"><nav class=\\\"crumbs\\\" aria-label=\\\"Breadcrumb\\\"><a href=\\\"../\\\">Home</a> / <a href=\\\"../services/\\\">Services</a> / <span>Fit-out &amp; joinery</span></nav><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Fit-out \u2014 Dubai &amp; UAE</p><h1>Fit-out and joinery shop drawings for <em>UAE interiors</em></h1><p>Joinery, ceiling, partition, kitchen and wardrobe drawings that a workshop can build from, coordinated with the stone and architectural sheets on the same project.</p></section><section class=\\\"section\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap split\\\"><figure><img src=\\\"../assets/img/drawings/elevation.svg\\\" alt=\\\"Joinery wall elevation drawing with cabinet units, shelves and a niche\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"300\\\" fetchpriority=\\\"high\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\"></figure><div class=\\\"copy\\\"><p>A fit-out shop drawing is the set a joiner, ceiling contractor or partition fixer can build from. The interior elevation shows the intent: a wardrobe, a slatted ceiling, a kitchen run. The shop drawing names the carcass, the finish, the hinge side, the shadow gap and the point where that unit meets stone, glass or gypsum. D3DDD prepares these sets in AutoCAD for fit-out contractors, joinery workshops and interior firms working in Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah and the other emirates.</p><p>The work is quoted per project after the drawings are reviewed. There is no day rate and no published price per sheet on this page. Send the interior elevations, the architectural plans and any site sizes you already have through the enquiry form.</p></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap copy\\\"><h2>What the issued set contains</h2><p>The usual issue is an AutoCAD DWG and a PDF of the same sheets. The DWG is the file the workshop keeps: real dimensions, layers, and piece marks that can be carried into a cutting list. The PDF is what the consultant marks up and what the site prints. Notes can be in English, Arabic or both. A revision table sits on the sheet so a later comment round is a new issue.</p><ul><li>Plans, interior elevations, sections and the enlarged details the units actually need.</li><li>Reflected ceiling plans with levels, bulkheads and access panels where the consultant drawing already shows them.</li><li>Partition types, heights and door openings, including the build-up where a partition meets stone or glass.</li><li>Kitchen and wardrobe elevations with carcass sizes, shelf spacing and the services they have to clear.</li><li>A note of hardware when you already know the hinge, runner or handle. Unknown hardware is left open, not invented.</li></ul><h2>Joinery elevations and sections</h2><p>Joinery drawings cover the units that are made off site and fixed on site. A wardrobe elevation shows width, height, depth, shelf spacing, hanging-rail height, and whether the door is hinged or sliding. A section shows the carcass thickness, the back panel, the plinth and the shadow gap against the wall. Where a stone top sits on a vanity, the joinery sheet stops at the carcass. The stone sheet, prepared with the marble shop drawings, carries the thickness, the edge and the sink cut-out. Keeping those two packages separate stops the stone yard pricing cabinet boxes and stops the joiner pricing a slab.</p><p>A wardrobe needs a plan of the niche, an elevation of each run, and a section through the hanging and shelf zones. If the walls are out of square, send the site sizes rather than a rectangle that will not fit.</p><h2>Ceilings and partitions</h2><p>Ceiling shop drawings set out the reflected plan: bulkhead lines, levels, access panels, and the relationship to lights, diffusers and sprinklers when those positions are already on the consultant drawing. D3DDD does not redesign the mechanical layout. If a diffuser clashes with a feature detail, the sheet flags the clash and the dimension that is blocked, and the revision waits until the consultant moves one of them. Partition drawings show type, height, door opening and the junction where a partition meets a stone jamb or a glass panel. Heights are taken from the architectural section you send. A missing finished-floor level is marked as open rather than guessed.</p><h2>Kitchens and the services behind them</h2><p>A kitchen elevation lines up the base units, tall units and wall units against the services: the sink, the hob, the fridge niche and the socket heights. Worktop thickness is noted so the stone package, if there is one, can use the same figure. Service points are traced from the drawing you send and are not moved unless you ask for that study.</p><h2>How the set is reviewed</h2><p>On fit-out projects in Dubai, Abu Dhabi and Sharjah the joinery and ceiling set is usually submitted by the contractor to the project consultant. The reviewer checks the sheets against the approved interior elevations: lines, heights, materials and the junctions between trades. Comments come back on the PDF or as a list. The next issue raises the revision and clouds what changed, so the workshop does not cut from a superseded sheet. D3DDD does not replace that consultant, and a shop drawing is not a building permit. Permit sets and BIM submissions are a different scope. If a project needs them, they are agreed separately, from the checklist you supply.</p><p>Turnaround is the date in the written quotation. One kitchen is not the same duration as a villa of wardrobes and a lobby ceiling. A missing site dimension pauses only the sheets it affects.</p><h2>What to send, and what sits beside this page</h2><p>Send the architectural plans, the interior elevations, any reflected ceiling plan, and photographs or a measured sketch of the rooms that are already built. Name the areas in scope. Broader CAD sets are under architectural drafting. Marble floors, vanities and cladding are on the marble shop drawings page, and the two packages can be quoted together. Quantities for joinery or stone are an estimation scope when you need a bill rather than a cutting list. The portfolio includes stone sheets that meet joinery, including a bathroom cladding set and vanity tops. Those are stone drawings, not cabinet drawings, and they show the junction both trades have to respect.</p></div></section><section class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"related\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Related</p><h2 class=\\\"mb-24\\\">Stone, drafting and sheets that meet the joinery</h2><div class=\\\"grid g3\\\"><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/architectural-drafting/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">CAD</span><h3>Architectural drafting</h3><p>The wider AutoCAD set around the fit-out package.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../marble.html\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">STONE</span><h3>Marble shop drawings</h3><p>Vanity tops, floors and cladding that meet the cabinets.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../interior-design-companies-uae/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">INT</span><h3>Interior design firms</h3><p>How a design elevation becomes a workshop set.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../construction-companies-uae/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">SITE</span><h3>Construction companies</h3><p>Fit-out documentation inside a contractor package.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/luxury-bathroom-marble-cladding-shop-drawings/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">BATH</span><h3>Bathroom cladding sheets</h3><p>Stone walls that stop where the joinery starts.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/paonazzetto-marble-vanity-tops-shop-drawings/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">TOP</span><h3>Vanity top sheets</h3><p>Stone tops that sit on a joinery carcass.</p></div></a></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt faq\\\" id=\\\"faq\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\"faq-h\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">FAQ</p><h2 id=\\\"faq-h\\\" class=\\\"mb-20\\\">Frequently asked questions</h2><details><summary>Do fit-out shop drawings include the marble top?</summary><p>The joinery sheet shows the carcass and the worktop thickness it has to accept. The stone plan, edge, cut-out and slab layout are marble shop drawings. Say if you want both in one quotation.</p></details><details><summary>Can you draw ceilings and partitions as well as kitchens?</summary><p>Yes, when they are in the scope. Ceiling sheets follow the reflected plan you send. Partition sheets show type, height and openings. Mechanical redesign is not part of the drawing.</p></details><details><summary>What files are delivered?</summary><p>AutoCAD DWG and PDF, with a revision table. Notes can be English, Arabic or both. A cutting list is added only when the quotation includes it.</p></details><details><summary>Is this a permit or a BIM submission?</summary><p>No. These are fabrication and installation sheets for the fit-out. A permit package or a BIM submission is a separate scope, and only from the checklist you send.</p></details></div></section><section class=\\\"cta-band\\\" id=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Have a Project</p><h2>Request a Project Quotation</h2><p>Send the drawings, sketches or scope you already have. The quotation confirms the price and the delivery date in writing before drafting starts.</p><div class=\\\"actions\\\"><a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"../contact.html?service=fitout\\\">Request a Project Quotation</a><span class=\\\"wa-contact\\\"><svg class=\\\"wa-ico\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"14\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path fill=\\\"currentColor\\\" d=\\\"M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z\\\"/></svg><span>WhatsApp: <bdi dir=\\\"ltr\\\">@mxhoaib</bdi></span></span></div></section>\", \"ld\": [{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Services\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/services/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Fit-out &amp; joinery\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/fitout-shop-drawings/\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"Service\", \"name\": \"Fit-out and joinery shop drawings\", \"description\": \"Joinery, ceiling, partition, kitchen and wardrobe shop drawings for fit-out projects in the UAE, issued as DWG and PDF.\", \"url\": \"https://d3ddd.com/fitout-shop-drawings/\", \"provider\": {\"@id\": \"https://d3ddd.com/#business\"}, \"areaServed\": [{\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Dubai\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Abu Dhabi\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Sharjah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ajman\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ras Al Khaimah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Umm Al Quwain\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Fujairah\"}, {\"@type\": \"Country\", \"name\": \"United Arab Emirates\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do fit-out shop drawings include the marble top?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The joinery sheet shows the carcass and the worktop thickness it has to accept. The stone plan, edge, cut-out and slab layout are marble shop drawings. Say if you want both in one quotation.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can you draw ceilings and partitions as well as kitchens?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes, when they are in the scope. Ceiling sheets follow the reflected plan you send. Partition sheets show type, height and openings. Mechanical redesign is not part of the drawing.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What files are delivered?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"AutoCAD DWG and PDF, with a revision table. Notes can be English, Arabic or both. A cutting list is added only when the quotation includes it.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is this a permit or a BIM submission?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. These are fabrication and installation sheets for the fit-out. A permit package or a BIM submission is a separate scope, and only from the checklist you send.\"}}]}], \"preload\": \"elevation\"}, {\"fn\": \"construction-companies-uae/index.html\", \"title\": \"Technical Drafting Support for UAE Contractors | D3DDD\", \"desc\": \"Technical drafting and design support for UAE construction companies: architectural, marble, fit-out, estimation and visualization packages in DWG and PDF.\", \"body\": \"<section class=\\\"page-hero\\\"><nav class=\\\"crumbs\\\" aria-label=\\\"Breadcrumb\\\"><a href=\\\"../\\\">Home</a> / <span>Industries</span> / <span>Construction companies</span></nav><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Contractors \u2014 Dubai &amp; UAE</p><h1>Technical Drafting &amp; Design Support for UAE Construction Companies</h1><p>Your Outsourced Architectural and Technical Drawing Partner.</p></section><section class=\\\"section\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap split\\\"><figure><img src=\\\"../assets/img/drawings/svc-drafting.svg\\\" alt=\\\"Architectural plan sheets and a CAD title block for contractor documentation\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"300\\\" fetchpriority=\\\"high\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\"></figure><div class=\\\"copy\\\"><p>Main contractors and fit-out contractors in the UAE often need drawing capacity between the consultant\u2019s design set and the workshops that will build. D3DDD prepares that layer: architectural documentation, marble and stone documentation, fit-out and interior documentation, and estimation or visualization when the same project needs numbers or a picture. The studio is in Dubai. Files go out as DWG and PDF to teams in Abu Dhabi, Sharjah and the other emirates. Nothing on this page is a claim about a particular contract, a named developer or a headcount.</p><p>You send the consultant drawings, the interior set, a marked-up PDF or a site sketch. The quotation names the areas, the price and the delivery date, and drafting starts after that is confirmed in writing. Shop drawings, estimation and 3D work are quoted per project. This page does not publish a rate per sheet or per square metre.</p></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap copy\\\"><h2>Architectural Documentation</h2><p>Architectural documentation here means the measured <a href=\\\"../services/architectural-drafting/\\\">AutoCAD drafting</a> work a site team can coordinate from: plans, elevations, sections, details and, when you ask for them, as-built sheets that record what was built. The set follows the title block and the layer names you already use if you send a sample. It is the package a contractor submits onward to the project consultant, not a replacement for that consultant and not a building permit. Permit-oriented sheets are prepared only from the checklist the project actually uses, because that checklist is not the same in every emirate.</p><ul><li>Plans, elevations, sections and the details the scope names.</li><li>As-built records for handover or a later alteration, from the survey or redlines you send.</li><li>Revision clouds and a revision table, so the site does not build from a mixed set.</li><li>English notes, with Arabic on request.</li></ul><h2>Marble &amp; Stone Documentation</h2><p>Stone is usually a specialist package inside the contractor\u2019s submission. The shop drawings name each piece, joint, thickness, edge and cut-out. Cutting lists and slab layouts follow when the yard has to nest the vein, and stone quantities are added when the quotation includes them. A floor, a stair, a vanity and a bookmatched wall each need their own information. The marble shop drawings page describes those deliverables in full. On this page the point is simpler: the contractor can send the interior elevations and ask for the stone set without hiring a separate drafter for that trade.</p><h2>Fit-Out &amp; Interior Documentation</h2><p>Fit-out and interior documentation covers the joinery, ceiling, partition and interior-elevation sheets that sit beside the architectural and stone sets. Kitchens and wardrobes are drawn so the carcass, the worktop thickness and the service points agree. Ceiling sheets follow the reflected plan you send and flag a clash instead of moving a diffuser. The fit-out shop drawings page is the longer description of that scope. A contractor who has both joinery and stone on one villa can ask for both in the same enquiry. They are still issued as separate packages so each workshop prices its own work.</p><h2>Estimation &amp; Visualization</h2><p>Estimation is the bill, the take-off or the material schedule measured from those drawings. Each line can name the sheet it came from, and assumptions such as joint width or cutting waste sit in the header. Visualization is the still image a client or a consultant looks at before they approve a material. A render is not a substitute for the dimensions. When both are in the quotation, the picture is described against the same design as the sheets, and an update after a comment round is its own line if the design actually changes. There is no published price per image and no published rate per page of a bill.</p><h2>Who We Support</h2><p>The enquiry can come from a main contractor\u2019s technical office, a fit-out contractor, a specialist subcontractor, or a site engineer who has been asked to get a trade package drawn. D3DDD does not publish a list of clients, and this page does not imply a framework agreement with any developer or contractor. Support means the drawings for the scope you send: one trade, one villa, or a package that spans architecture, stone and joinery. If you already have an in-house drafter, the studio can take the overflow trade, such as the stone or the joinery, and leave the rest of the set with your team.</p><h2>Project Workflow</h2><p>The workflow is the same five steps whether the site is in Dubai or in another emirate, because the files move by email. A comment from the consultant is not a new mystery process. It is step four, and the delivery of that revision is agreed when the comments are in hand.</p><ol class=\\\"steps mt-14\\\"><li>Send the project drawings and the scope.</li><li>We review them and confirm the quotation in writing.</li><li>The first issue is drafted as DWG and PDF.</li><li>You and your consultant comment.</li><li>The approved issue is delivered for fabrication or for the next submission.</li></ol><p>Missing dimensions pause only the sheets they affect. A large change of scope, such as adding a floor that was not in the quotation, is priced before it is drawn. The portfolio shows the kind of contractor-facing stone sheets already issued for Dubai villas, including a ground-floor flooring layout and the external pool and majlis details. They are examples of drawing habit, not a client roster.</p></div></section><section class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"related\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Related</p><h2 class=\\\"mb-24\\\">The services and sheets a contractor package uses</h2><div class=\\\"grid g3\\\"><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/architectural-drafting/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">CAD</span><h3>Architectural drafting</h3><p>Shop drawings, as-built sets and CAD detailing.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../marble.html\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">STONE</span><h3>Marble shop drawings</h3><p>Fabrication drawings, cutting lists and slab layouts.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../fitout-shop-drawings/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">FIT</span><h3>Fit-out and joinery</h3><p>Ceilings, partitions, kitchens and wardrobes.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/architectural-estimation/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">BOQ</span><h3>Estimation and BOQ</h3><p>Bills and material schedules from the drawings.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/villa-ground-floor-marble-flooring-layout/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">PLAN</span><h3>Villa floor layout</h3><p>A ground-floor stone set-out for a residential package.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/villa-swimming-pool-and-outdoor-majlis-tiling-details/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">POOL</span><h3>Pool and outdoor tiling</h3><p>Plans, sections and details for external works.</p></div></a></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt faq\\\" id=\\\"faq\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\"faq-h\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">FAQ</p><h2 id=\\\"faq-h\\\" class=\\\"mb-20\\\">Frequently asked questions</h2><details><summary>Can one quotation cover stone and joinery?</summary><p>Yes. Say so on the form. The packages are still issued separately so the stone yard and the joiner each receive their own sheets.</p></details><details><summary>Do you replace our consultant?</summary><p>No. The drawings are prepared for your submission. Approval to fabricate or to build remains with the reviewer named on your project.</p></details><details><summary>Which emirates can send work?</summary><p>Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, Ajman, Ras Al Khaimah, Umm Al Quwain and Fujairah. Delivery is digital.</p></details><details><summary>What do we receive?</summary><p>DWG and PDF for drawings. A spreadsheet as well when the quotation includes a bill or a cutting list. PNG or JPG when the quotation includes stills.</p></details></div></section><section class=\\\"cta-band\\\" id=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Have a Project</p><h2>Request a Project Quotation</h2><p>Send the drawings, sketches or scope you already have. The quotation confirms the price and the delivery date in writing before drafting starts.</p><div class=\\\"actions\\\"><a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"../contact.html?service=drafting\\\">Request a Project Quotation</a><span class=\\\"wa-contact\\\"><svg class=\\\"wa-ico\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"14\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path fill=\\\"currentColor\\\" d=\\\"M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z\\\"/></svg><span>WhatsApp: <bdi dir=\\\"ltr\\\">@mxhoaib</bdi></span></span></div></section>\", \"ld\": [{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Construction companies\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/construction-companies-uae/\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"Service\", \"name\": \"Technical drafting support for UAE construction companies\", \"description\": \"Outsourced architectural documentation, marble and stone drawings, fit-out sheets, estimation and visualization for contractors in the UAE.\", \"url\": \"https://d3ddd.com/construction-companies-uae/\", \"provider\": {\"@id\": \"https://d3ddd.com/#business\"}, \"areaServed\": [{\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Dubai\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Abu Dhabi\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Sharjah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ajman\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ras Al Khaimah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Umm Al Quwain\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Fujairah\"}, {\"@type\": \"Country\", \"name\": \"United Arab Emirates\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can one quotation cover stone and joinery?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. Say so on the form. The packages are still issued separately so the stone yard and the joiner each receive their own sheets.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do you replace our consultant?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. The drawings are prepared for your submission. Approval to fabricate or to build remains with the reviewer named on your project.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which emirates can send work?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah, Ajman, Ras Al Khaimah, Umm Al Quwain and Fujairah. Delivery is digital.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What do we receive?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"DWG and PDF for drawings. A spreadsheet as well when the quotation includes a bill or a cutting list. PNG or JPG when the quotation includes stills.\"}}]}], \"preload\": \"svc-drafting\"}, {\"fn\": \"real-estate-developers-uae/index.html\", \"title\": \"3D Visualization for UAE Real Estate Developers | D3DDD\", \"desc\": \"3D visualization for UAE real-estate teams: presentation stills, material studies and design-coordination views. Shop drawings quoted separately.\", \"body\": \"<section class=\\\"page-hero\\\"><nav class=\\\"crumbs\\\" aria-label=\\\"Breadcrumb\\\"><a href=\\\"../\\\">Home</a> / <span>Industries</span> / <span>Real estate developers</span></nav><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Developers \u2014 Dubai &amp; UAE</p><h1>3D visualization for real estate <em>project teams</em> in the UAE</h1><p>Presentation stills, material studies and design-coordination views for teams who need to see a space before they approve a drawing. The picture does not replace the shop drawings.</p></section><section class=\\\"section\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap split\\\"><figure><img src=\\\"../assets/img/drawings/svc-3d.svg\\\" alt=\\\"Isometric room and camera study for an architectural visualization\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"300\\\" fetchpriority=\\\"high\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\"></figure><div class=\\\"copy\\\"><p>A development team often has to show a lobby, a typical apartment or a villa majlis before the shop drawings are finished. A still render can carry the vein direction, the joinery colour and the light well enough for that meeting. It cannot be measured with a tape, and it should not be the document a factory cuts from. D3DDD builds those images from the drawings you send, for project teams working in Dubai and across the UAE.</p><p>This page is about visualization, presentations and design coordination. It is not a marketing retainer, and it does not claim placements, sales results or a relationship with any developer. The images are quoted per view or per space after the brief is clear. There is no price per image on this site.</p></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap copy\\\"><h2>What a presentation still is for</h2><p>A presentation still is a decision picture. It is useful when a project team, a sales gallery or an internal design review needs to compare two stones, two joinery colours or two ceiling heights. The quotation names the number of views. A lobby, a living room and a close-up of a marble wall are three views, not an open-ended set of \u201cenough images\u201d. An extra view later is priced on its own. If the slabs arrive and the vein does not match the picture, the picture was a study. The supply contract is still the approved shop drawing and the stone that was actually delivered.</p><p>Files are PNG or JPG at the resolution written in the quotation. A model file is included only if you ask for it, for example so another office can place a camera later. A short walkthrough is a separate line, not an assumption that every still comes with a film. Notes can point back to the drawing sheet the camera was taken from, so the picture does not drift away from the plan.</p><h2>Design coordination, not a substitute for dimensions</h2><p>Design coordination views are the images that show a junction: stone meeting joinery, a ceiling bulkhead against a curtain wall, a vanity against a fluted wall. They are useful because a plan hides that corner. They are dangerous if the corner in the picture uses a thickness the drawings do not. When visualization and shop drawings are in the same quotation, the image follows the joint logic of the sheets. When only the image is commissioned, it is labelled as a study based on the drawings you sent, and those drawings may still change.</p><p>In Dubai, Abu Dhabi and Sharjah a client meeting may approve the look weeks before the consultant approves the shop drawings for fabrication. If a splash height or a niche moves in the approved drawing and the picture is not updated, the site is showing an image that is no longer true. An update of the still is described in the quotation rather than assumed. D3DDD does not treat a render as an authority submission or as a permit.</p><h2>What the model is built from</h2><p>The model needs a plan, even a sketch with approximate sizes, before it is worth building. Photographs of the space help. If the stone has already been delivered, photographs of the slabs help the vein. Materials you are still choosing can be shown as options: two stones, or a stone and a timber, in the same camera. Inventing a floor plate, a view or a neighbouring building that you did not send is not part of the work. If a drawing is missing, that part of the image waits or is shown as a simple mass, and the quotation says which.</p><h2>How this sits with the rest of the studio</h2><p>Architectural design is the earlier plan work: layouts, space planning and elevations in DWG, so a later shop drawing does not have to be traced from a picture. Marble shop drawings are the fabrication set for floors, vanities, stairs and cladding. Fit-out drawings cover the joinery the image is showing. A developer\u2019s technical office can ask for the stills first and the sheets second, or the other way around. They are different deliverables. The <a href=\\\"../services/3d-rendering-modeling-visualization/\\\">3D rendering in Dubai</a> service lists the file types in more detail.</p><p>The portfolio is shop drawings rather than a gallery of marketing renders. The entrance-lobby medallion and the villa ground-floor layout are useful references because they are the kind of stone geometry a presentation still has to respect: a radial hall, a waterjet centre, a numbered slab set-out. Look at them before you brief a view of a similar floor. They are issued sheets with client marks removed, not a claim that the studio produced a sales campaign.</p><h2>What to send for a quotation</h2><p>Send the plans or sketches, the materials you are considering, the rooms or elevations you need to see, and whether the images are for an internal review or for a presentation you will show onward. Name the emirate if the review context matters, even though the files themselves are delivered digitally. A deadline belongs in the same note. The date is confirmed with the price, before any modelling starts. Comment rounds on the images are further issues once your marked-up PDF or your written notes arrive.</p></div></section><section class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"related\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Related</p><h2 class=\\\"mb-24\\\">Drawings and examples that keep the picture honest</h2><div class=\\\"grid g3\\\"><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/3d-rendering-modeling-visualization/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">3D</span><h3>3D visualization</h3><p>Stills, material options and walkthroughs when scoped.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/architectural-designing/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">DES</span><h3>Architectural design</h3><p>Layouts and elevations the model is built from.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../marble.html\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">STONE</span><h3>Marble shop drawings</h3><p>The measured stone set a render must not invent.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../interior-design-companies-uae/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">INT</span><h3>Interior firms</h3><p>Joinery and material coordination beside the images.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/entrance-lobby-waterjet-marble-medallion-flooring/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">LOBBY</span><h3>Lobby medallion floor</h3><p>A feature floor of the kind a presentation still would show.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/villa-ground-floor-marble-flooring-layout/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">PLAN</span><h3>Villa floor layout</h3><p>The plan a coordination view should agree with.</p></div></a></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt faq\\\" id=\\\"faq\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\"faq-h\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">FAQ</p><h2 id=\\\"faq-h\\\" class=\\\"mb-20\\\">Frequently asked questions</h2><details><summary>Will the renders be enough to fabricate from?</summary><p>No. Fabrication needs DWG and PDF shop drawings with dimensions, joints and cut-outs. The still is for the decision about the look.</p></details><details><summary>Can you show more than one material?</summary><p>Yes. The quotation states how many options and how many cameras. Two stones in one view is a different scope from two fully different rooms.</p></details><details><summary>Do you produce the sales brochure as well?</summary><p>No. The deliverable is the stills, and a model or a walkthrough only if the quotation says so. Layout of a brochure is not part of this service.</p></details><details><summary>Which drawings should we send first?</summary><p>The plans and the elevations you want the camera to follow. If those are still sketches, the image is labelled as a study.</p></details></div></section><section class=\\\"cta-band\\\" id=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Have a Project</p><h2>Request a Project Quotation</h2><p>Send the drawings, sketches or scope you already have. The quotation confirms the price and the delivery date in writing before drafting starts.</p><div class=\\\"actions\\\"><a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"../contact.html?service=3d\\\">Request a Project Quotation</a><span class=\\\"wa-contact\\\"><svg class=\\\"wa-ico\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"14\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path fill=\\\"currentColor\\\" d=\\\"M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z\\\"/></svg><span>WhatsApp: <bdi dir=\\\"ltr\\\">@mxhoaib</bdi></span></span></div></section>\", \"ld\": [{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Real estate developers\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/real-estate-developers-uae/\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"Service\", \"name\": \"3D visualization for UAE real estate developers\", \"description\": \"Interior and exterior stills, presentation images and design-coordination views for real estate project teams in the UAE.\", \"url\": \"https://d3ddd.com/real-estate-developers-uae/\", \"provider\": {\"@id\": \"https://d3ddd.com/#business\"}, \"areaServed\": [{\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Dubai\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Abu Dhabi\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Sharjah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ajman\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ras Al Khaimah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Umm Al Quwain\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Fujairah\"}, {\"@type\": \"Country\", \"name\": \"United Arab Emirates\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Will the renders be enough to fabricate from?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. Fabrication needs DWG and PDF shop drawings with dimensions, joints and cut-outs. The still is for the decision about the look.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can you show more than one material?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. The quotation states how many options and how many cameras. Two stones in one view is a different scope from two fully different rooms.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do you produce the sales brochure as well?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. The deliverable is the stills, and a model or a walkthrough only if the quotation says so. Layout of a brochure is not part of this service.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which drawings should we send first?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The plans and the elevations you want the camera to follow. If those are still sketches, the image is labelled as a study.\"}}]}], \"preload\": \"svc-3d\"}, {\"fn\": \"interior-design-companies-uae/index.html\", \"title\": \"Interior Drawings for UAE Design Firms | D3DDD\", \"desc\": \"Interior renders, joinery shop drawings and material coordination for UAE interior design firms. DWG, PDF and stills, quoted per project.\", \"body\": \"<section class=\\\"page-hero\\\"><nav class=\\\"crumbs\\\" aria-label=\\\"Breadcrumb\\\"><a href=\\\"../\\\">Home</a> / <span>Industries</span> / <span>Interior design firms</span></nav><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Interiors \u2014 Dubai &amp; UAE</p><h1>Interior drawings and renders for <em>UAE design firms</em></h1><p>Interior renders, joinery shop drawings and material coordination for firms that design the room and need someone else to draw it for the workshop.</p></section><section class=\\\"section\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap split\\\"><figure><img src=\\\"../assets/img/drawings/kitchen.svg\\\" alt=\\\"Kitchen cabinet elevation line drawing used to coordinate joinery and finishes\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"300\\\" fetchpriority=\\\"high\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\"></figure><div class=\\\"copy\\\"><p>An interior design firm usually owns the look: the elevation, the finish, the way a wardrobe meets a marble jamb. The workshop owns the making. The gap between those two is a shop drawing. D3DDD draws that gap for interior firms in Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah and the rest of the UAE: joinery elevations, material notes that match the stone package, and stills when the client needs to see the finish before the factory cuts.</p><p>The firm stays the designer. These drawings do not appoint D3DDD as the project\u2019s interior consultant, and they are not a permit set. Fees are per project. Send the elevations, the plans and a note of which rooms are in scope.</p></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap copy\\\"><h2>From a design elevation to a joinery sheet</h2><p>A design elevation is allowed to be beautiful and slightly incomplete. A joinery sheet is not. It needs the niche size, the finished floor, the plinth, the hinge side and the shadow gap. Where your elevation already has those, the shop drawing follows them and adds the sections a workshop asks for. Where a dimension is missing, that part of the sheet is flagged and left until you send it. Guessing a carcass depth to make the drawing look finished is how a wardrobe fails to fit.</p><p>Kitchens, wardrobes, vanities and feature panelling are the usual scope. Ceiling and partition drawings are included when they are part of the same interior package. The longer description of those sheet types is on the fit-out shop drawings page. Hardware is noted when the specification already names it. If the handle is still a client choice, the elevation shows the position and the length as \u201cto be confirmed\u201d rather than a made-up code.</p><h2>Material coordination with stone</h2><p>Interior projects in the UAE often fail at the line where timber meets stone. The vanity carcass, the stone top, the splash and the wall cladding can be drawn by three people who never shared a thickness. Material coordination means those thicknesses are written once and used on every sheet. The joinery elevation states the top thickness it is built for. The marble shop drawing states the same thickness, the edge and the cut-out. If they disagree, the set is not issued until you choose one.</p><p>Bookmatching, a fluted stone panel or a waterjet floor is a stone decision, not a joinery decision. The interior elevation can show the intent. The slab layout shows whether the slabs you have can do it. That layout lives with the marble drawings. An interior firm can ask for both in one enquiry. The files still go to the right workshop: DWG and PDF of joinery to the joiner, DWG and PDF of stone to the yard.</p><h2>Interior renders that match the elevations</h2><p>A render is useful when your client has approved a sketch but has not understood the material. One camera of the room, with the stone and the joinery you specified, is often enough. A second camera is a second view in the quotation, not a free extra. The image is built from your elevations. If those elevations later change the splash height, the image is out of date until it is updated, and that update is a separate line if it was not included.</p><p>The still is PNG or JPG. It is not the file the joiner cuts from. Interior firms who want the picture and the sheets should say so at the start, so the cameras and the drawings describe the same junctions. The <a href=\\\"../services/3d-rendering-modeling-visualization/\\\">3D rendering in Dubai</a> page explains what a still can and cannot prove. Lighting in the image is presentation lighting. It is not a lighting calculation and it is not a claim that a fitting schedule has been coordinated.</p><h2>How comments usually travel</h2><p>On many interior projects the designer comments first, because the look is theirs, and the project consultant comments later, because the fabrication is the contractor\u2019s submission. Those are two different mark-ups. D3DDD revises against the notes you forward. The revision number goes up so the workshop does not build an earlier PDF that is still in someone\u2019s inbox. Title blocks differ between Dubai, Abu Dhabi and Sharjah practices. Send yours if the sheets have to match a consultant template.</p><p>Turnaround is agreed in the quotation. A pair of vanities is a smaller set than a full apartment of joinery. Arabic or English notes, or both, are a normal request. Say which language the workshop and the consultant actually read.</p><h2>Examples that show the stone side of an interior</h2><p>The published projects are stone shop drawings, which is the half of an interior package that is often missing when the joinery is already drawn. A Venatino bath vanity and a bathroom cladding set show edges, mitres and niches of the kind an interior elevation has to leave room for. Use them as a reference for the level of dimensioning, not as a claim that the studio designed those rooms. If you need the joinery half as well, that is this page and the fit-out page.</p></div></section><section class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"related\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Related</p><h2 class=\\\"mb-24\\\">The services an interior package usually splits into</h2><div class=\\\"grid g3\\\"><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../fitout-shop-drawings/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">FIT</span><h3>Fit-out and joinery drawings</h3><p>Ceilings, partitions, kitchens and wardrobes.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/3d-rendering-modeling-visualization/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">3D</span><h3>3D visualization</h3><p>Stills for the material and the light.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../marble.html\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">STONE</span><h3>Marble shop drawings</h3><p>Floors, vanities and cladding coordinated with the joinery.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/architectural-designing/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">DES</span><h3>Architectural design</h3><p>Plan options before the elevations are frozen.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/venatino-marble-bath-vanity-shop-drawing/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">VAN</span><h3>Bath vanity sheet</h3><p>A stone vanity the joinery has to carry.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/luxury-bathroom-marble-cladding-shop-drawings/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">BATH</span><h3>Bathroom cladding</h3><p>Wall stone coordinated with niches and grooves.</p></div></a></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt faq\\\" id=\\\"faq\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\"faq-h\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">FAQ</p><h2 id=\\\"faq-h\\\" class=\\\"mb-20\\\">Frequently asked questions</h2><details><summary>Can you work from our elevations only?</summary><p>Yes, if they are complete enough to dimension. Missing sizes are flagged. A sketch with site measures is better than an elevation that was never checked.</p></details><details><summary>Will you specify the finishes for us?</summary><p>The sheets record the finishes you have already chosen. Choosing the concept is the designer\u2019s work. Coordinating the thickness between joinery and stone is part of the drawing.</p></details><details><summary>Can the same enquiry include renders?</summary><p>Yes. State the views. The stills and the shop drawings are both named in the quotation so one does not get assumed inside the other.</p></details><details><summary>Do you issue one file for every trade?</summary><p>No. Joinery, stone and ceilings are separate packages even when they are quoted together, so each workshop receives its own sheets.</p></details></div></section><section class=\\\"cta-band\\\" id=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Have a Project</p><h2>Request a Project Quotation</h2><p>Send the drawings, sketches or scope you already have. The quotation confirms the price and the delivery date in writing before drafting starts.</p><div class=\\\"actions\\\"><a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"../contact.html?service=fitout\\\">Request a Project Quotation</a><span class=\\\"wa-contact\\\"><svg class=\\\"wa-ico\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"14\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path fill=\\\"currentColor\\\" d=\\\"M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z\\\"/></svg><span>WhatsApp: <bdi dir=\\\"ltr\\\">@mxhoaib</bdi></span></span></div></section>\", \"ld\": [{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Interior design firms\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/interior-design-companies-uae/\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"Service\", \"name\": \"Interior design and joinery drawings for UAE interior firms\", \"description\": \"Joinery shop drawings, interior elevations, material coordination and interior renders for interior design firms in the UAE.\", \"url\": \"https://d3ddd.com/interior-design-companies-uae/\", \"provider\": {\"@id\": \"https://d3ddd.com/#business\"}, \"areaServed\": [{\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Dubai\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Abu Dhabi\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Sharjah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ajman\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ras Al Khaimah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Umm Al Quwain\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Fujairah\"}, {\"@type\": \"Country\", \"name\": \"United Arab Emirates\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can you work from our elevations only?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes, if they are complete enough to dimension. Missing sizes are flagged. A sketch with site measures is better than an elevation that was never checked.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Will you specify the finishes for us?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"The sheets record the finishes you have already chosen. Choosing the concept is the designer\u2019s work. Coordinating the thickness between joinery and stone is part of the drawing.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can the same enquiry include renders?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes. State the views. The stills and the shop drawings are both named in the quotation so one does not get assumed inside the other.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do you issue one file for every trade?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. Joinery, stone and ceilings are separate packages even when they are quoted together, so each workshop receives its own sheets.\"}}]}], \"preload\": \"kitchen\"}, {\"fn\": \"marble-contractors-uae/index.html\", \"title\": \"Stone Shop Drawings for UAE Contractors | D3DDD\", \"desc\": \"Stone shop drawings, slab layouts, cutting lists and stone quantities for UAE marble contractors. AutoCAD DWG and PDF, quoted per project.\", \"body\": \"<section class=\\\"page-hero\\\"><nav class=\\\"crumbs\\\" aria-label=\\\"Breadcrumb\\\"><a href=\\\"../\\\">Home</a> / <span>Industries</span> / <span>Marble contractors</span></nav><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Stone yards \u2014 Dubai &amp; UAE</p><h1>Stone shop drawings and slab layouts for <em>UAE marble contractors</em></h1><p>Fabrication drawings, slab layouts, cutting lists and stone quantities for yards that have to nest a vein and cut a piece only once.</p></section><section class=\\\"section\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap split\\\"><figure><img src=\\\"../assets/img/drawings/marble-shop-drawing.svg\\\" alt=\\\"Marble countertop shop drawing with joints, a sink cut-out and an edge-profile section\\\" width=\\\"400\\\" height=\\\"300\\\" fetchpriority=\\\"high\\\" decoding=\\\"async\\\"></figure><div class=\\\"copy\\\"><p>A marble contractor does not need another mood board. The yard needs a sheet that says which piece is cut from which slab, which edge is mitred, and which opening is for the sink. D3DDD draws that set for stone workshops and marble contractors in Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Sharjah and the other emirates. The longer description of the deliverables is on the <a href=\\\"../marble.html\\\">marble shop drawings service</a>. The <a href=\\\"../blog/what-are-marble-shop-drawings/\\\">Marble Shop Drawings Guide (UAE)</a> maps the checklists, edges, stairs and project sheets around that set. Compare sheets on <a href=\\\"../projects/\\\">selected stone projects</a>. This page is about how a yard uses the set: shop drawings, slab layouts, cutting lists and stone quantities.</p><p>The price is quoted per project after the drawings, the slab photos or the interior elevations are reviewed. There is no rate card. Send what you have. A deadline matters, because a pair of vanity tops is not a villa floor.</p></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap copy\\\"><h2>Shop drawings the bridge saw can follow</h2><p>The shop drawing is the fabrication and installation set for one job. A countertop needs a plan, the joint, the thickness, the edge profile and every cut-out. A stair needs treads, risers and the fixing the interior elevation will not show. A bookmatched wall needs the elevation and the sequence of panels. Each of those is drawn in AutoCAD and issued as DWG and PDF. The DWG is the file the factory keeps. The PDF is the file the consultant marks and the site prints. Arabic notes can sit beside the English ones if the workshop or the consultant reads Arabic.</p><p>Piece marks on the drawing match the cutting list. A mark that exists on the elevation and not on the list, or the other way around, is a mistake the yard will find on the saw. The first issue is checked for that match before it is sent. A revision, after your comments or the consultant\u2019s, raises the number so nobody cuts from the superseded PDF.</p><h2>Slab layouts</h2><p>A slab layout is the plan of which piece comes from which slab so the vein continues and the waste is visible. It is not the same drawing as the floor plan. The floor plan shows the room. The slab layout shows the raw slab, the pieces nested on it, and the direction of the vein. Bookmatching is drawn when the design depends on it, and it is left out when the stone is a plain field and matching would only waste material. If you already have the slabs, send photographs with a scale. Nesting on a generic rectangle is less useful than nesting on the slab you will actually cut.</p><p>Two published sheets show the habit. One nests numbered bathroom panels on slab photos. Another nests Fusion Blue door frames, lintels and skirting so each piece follows the vein. They are real sets with client marks removed. Use them to see the level of the drawing, not as a promise that every project looks like a villa bathroom.</p><h2>Cutting lists</h2><p>The cutting list is the schedule the saw operator and the buyer can both read. Each line carries the piece mark, the finished size, the thickness, the edge, the material and the slab it is nested on. Units stay visible: millimetres for the piece, square metres where an area is being ordered. A list that only says \u201cvanity\u201d without a mark is not a cutting list. If the workshop uses its own column order, send an empty template and the list will follow it.</p><ul><li>Piece marks that match the shop drawings and the slab layout.</li><li>Finished sizes, thickness, edge and the cut-outs that change the blank.</li><li>The slab number, so the yard does not recut a piece from the wrong block.</li><li>A note of pieces still on hold because a site size is missing.</li></ul><h2>Stone quantities</h2><p>Quantities are useful when someone has to order, and they are misleading when they hide the waste. Areas, linear metres of skirting and a count of sink cut-outs are measured from the sheets. The cutting-waste assumption is written in the header of the schedule, not buried in a cell, so the person pricing the job can change it if the yard\u2019s policy is different. Stone quantities can sit inside the marble package or be part of a wider bill under <a href=\\\"../services/architectural-estimation/\\\">architectural estimation and quantity take-off</a>. They are not added silently. A full tender bill for every trade is a different quotation from a stone schedule for one bathroom.</p><p>When a comment changes a thickness or a height, the quantity moves with the revision or the order will not match the approved sheet. That update is included when the quotation says so. A redesign of the whole floor is quoted as its own step.</p><h2>What the yard should send</h2><p>Send the interior elevations or architectural plans, the stone name and thickness if you know them, slab photos when the vein matters, and the areas in scope. If the joinery is being drawn as well, say so. The carcass is a fit-out drawing. The top is a stone drawing. Contractors who are sending the package on the yard\u2019s behalf can use the construction-companies page. The same five-step workflow applies: send, written quotation, first issue, comments, delivery of DWG and PDF. Consultant approval in Dubai, Abu Dhabi or Sharjah is the reviewer\u2019s, against whatever checklist that project uses. The shop drawing is not a municipal permit.</p></div></section><section class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"related\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Related</p><h2 class=\\\"mb-24\\\">The marble page and the sheets a yard can compare</h2><div class=\\\"grid g3\\\"><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../marble.html\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">STONE</span><h3>Marble shop drawings</h3><p>The full description of fabrication drawings and BOQ.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../services/architectural-estimation/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">BOQ</span><h3>Estimation and BOQ</h3><p>Quantities and waste assumptions written so a buyer can check them.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../fitout-shop-drawings/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">FIT</span><h3>Fit-out and joinery</h3><p>The carcass and ceiling sheets the stone has to meet.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../construction-companies-uae/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">SITE</span><h3>Construction companies</h3><p>When the contractor, not the yard, is sending the package.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/marble-slab-cutting-layout-bathroom-cladding/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">NEST</span><h3>Bathroom slab nesting</h3><p>Numbered panels set out on real slab photos.</p></div></a><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"../projects/fusion-blue-marble-door-frame-and-skirting-slab-layout/\\\"><div class=\\\"b\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">FRAME</span><h3>Door frames and skirting</h3><p>Pieces nested so the vein continues through the frame.</p></div></a></div></div></section><section class=\\\"section alt faq\\\" id=\\\"faq\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\"faq-h\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">FAQ</p><h2 id=\\\"faq-h\\\" class=\\\"mb-20\\\">Frequently asked questions</h2><details><summary>Do you nest on our actual slabs?</summary><p>Yes, when you send slab photos or dimensions. A layout on a generic rectangle is only used if the real slabs are not known yet, and it is labelled that way.</p></details><details><summary>Is the cutting list the same file as the drawing?</summary><p>No. The drawings are DWG and PDF. The cutting list is a schedule, spreadsheet-ready when it is included in the quotation, with marks that match the sheets.</p></details><details><summary>Can you quantity the stone without redrawing it?</summary><p>Yes, if the drawings you already have are complete enough to measure. Missing elevations are marked as not measured, not filled with a guess.</p></details><details><summary>Which projects can we look at first?</summary><p>Start with the marble shop drawings page, then the bathroom slab-nesting set and the Fusion Blue door-frame layout. Both are in the portfolio.</p></details></div></section><section class=\\\"cta-band\\\" id=\\\"quote\\\"><p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Have a Project</p><h2>Request a Project Quotation</h2><p>Send the drawings, sketches or scope you already have. The quotation confirms the price and the delivery date in writing before drafting starts.</p><div class=\\\"actions\\\"><a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"../contact.html?service=marble\\\">Request a Project Quotation</a><span class=\\\"wa-contact\\\"><svg class=\\\"wa-ico\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\" width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"14\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path fill=\\\"currentColor\\\" d=\\\"M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413Z\\\"/></svg><span>WhatsApp: <bdi dir=\\\"ltr\\\">@mxhoaib</bdi></span></span></div></section>\", \"ld\": [{\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Marble contractors\", \"item\": \"https://d3ddd.com/marble-contractors-uae/\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"Service\", \"name\": \"Stone shop drawings and slab layouts for UAE marble contractors\", \"description\": \"Shop drawings, slab layouts, cutting lists and stone quantities for marble and stone contractors in the UAE.\", \"url\": \"https://d3ddd.com/marble-contractors-uae/\", \"provider\": {\"@id\": \"https://d3ddd.com/#business\"}, \"areaServed\": [{\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Dubai\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Abu Dhabi\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Sharjah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ajman\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Ras Al Khaimah\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Umm Al Quwain\"}, {\"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Fujairah\"}, {\"@type\": \"Country\", \"name\": \"United Arab Emirates\"}]}, {\"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do you nest on our actual slabs?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes, when you send slab photos or dimensions. A layout on a generic rectangle is only used if the real slabs are not known yet, and it is labelled that way.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Is the cutting list the same file as the drawing?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No. The drawings are DWG and PDF. The cutting list is a schedule, spreadsheet-ready when it is included in the quotation, with marks that match the sheets.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can you quantity the stone without redrawing it?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes, if the drawings you already have are complete enough to measure. Missing elevations are marked as not measured, not filled with a guess.\"}}, {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Which projects can we look at first?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Start with the marble shop drawings page, then the bathroom slab-nesting set and the Fusion Blue door-frame layout. Both are in the portfolio.\"}}]}], \"preload\": \"marble-shop-drawing\"}]")

def _expand_fitout(item):
    """Append the fit-out distinction copy, FAQs and Service offer. Title, meta and H1 stay."""
    if item["fn"] != "fitout-shop-drawings/index.html":
        return
    section = (
        "<h2>How fit-out drawings sit next to architectural drafting and marble</h2>"
        "<p><a href=\"../fitout-shop-drawings/\">Fit-out and joinery shop drawings</a> are the interior package: "
        "ceilings, partitions, kitchens, wardrobes and interior elevations, issued as AutoCAD DWG and PDF, with a revision table. "
        "Notes can be English, Arabic or both. They are a focused part of the wider "
        "<a href=\"../services/architectural-drafting/\">architectural drafting</a> offer. "
        "Use this page when the scope is the interior fit-out or the joinery workshop set. "
        "Use the drafting page when you also need as-built records, a broader construction-drawing set, or permit-oriented sheets prepared from your checklist.</p>"
        "<p>The live FAQ already draws that line clearly. These are fabrication and installation sheets for the fit-out. "
        "A permit package or a BIM submission is a separate scope, and only from the checklist you send. "
        "Ceiling sheets follow the reflected plan you send. Partition sheets show type, height and openings. Mechanical redesign is not part of the drawing.</p>"
        "<p>Where stone meets the cabinets — vanity tops, cladding that stops at a carcass, worktop thickness — the joinery sheet and the "
        "<a href=\"../marble.html\">marble shop drawings</a> have to agree. The joinery sheet shows the carcass and the worktop thickness it has to accept; "
        "the stone plan, edge, cut-out and slab layout stay on the marble page. Both can be quoted together when you say so in the enquiry. "
        "Published sheets that meet this junction include the <a href=\"../projects/luxury-bathroom-marble-cladding-shop-drawings/\">bathroom cladding</a> "
        "and <a href=\"../projects/paonazzetto-marble-vanity-tops-shop-drawings/\">Paonazzetto vanity tops</a> projects.</p>"
        "<p>Quantities for a tender or an order are measured under <a href=\"../services/architectural-estimation/\">architectural estimation</a> "
        "and should follow the same drawing revision. If a client needs to see a kitchen, wardrobe or ceiling before they approve the workshop set, "
        "<a href=\"../services/3d-rendering-modeling-visualization/\">3D modeling and rendering</a> can be quoted alongside; a picture does not replace the DWG.</p>"
        "<p>Fit-out drawings are quoted per project. Scope, fee and delivery date are confirmed in writing before drafting starts. "
        "Send the interior or joinery set through the <a href=\"../contact.html\">contact form</a>.</p>"
    )
    marker = "</div></section><section class=\"section\" id=\"related\">"
    if marker not in item["body"]:
        raise SystemExit("fit-out copy marker missing")
    item["body"] = item["body"].replace(marker, section + marker, 1)
    faqs = [
        ("How do fit-out shop drawings differ from architectural drafting?",
         "Fit-out and joinery shop drawings are the interior and workshop sheets (ceilings, partitions, kitchens, wardrobes, interior elevations). Architectural drafting is the wider AutoCAD service, including construction drawings, as-built and, when scoped, permit-oriented sets. You can request either, or both in one quote."),
        ("Do fit-out drawings include marble cutting lists?",
         "Only when the quotation includes them. Stone plans, edges, cut-outs and slab layouts are marble shop drawings."),
        ("Are these drawings issued as AutoCAD files?",
         "Yes. AutoCAD DWG and PDF, with a revision table, as the live page already states. Notes can be English, Arabic or both."),
        ("Can fit-out drawings and a quantity take-off be quoted together?",
         "Yes. Say so in the enquiry. The take-off is prepared on the estimation service and should follow the same drawing revision."),
    ]
    details = "".join("<details><summary>%s</summary><p>%s</p></details>" % pair for pair in (
        (faqs[0][0], faqs[0][1].replace(
            "Architectural drafting",
            "<a href=\"../services/architectural-drafting/\">Architectural drafting</a>",
            1,
        )),
        (faqs[1][0], faqs[1][1].replace(
            "marble shop drawings",
            "<a href=\"../marble.html\">marble shop drawings</a>",
            1,
        )),
        faqs[2],
        (faqs[3][0], faqs[3][1].replace(
            "estimation",
            "<a href=\"../services/architectural-estimation/\">estimation</a>",
            1,
        )),
    ))
    faq_marker = "</div></section><section class=\"cta-band\""
    if faq_marker not in item["body"]:
        raise SystemExit("fit-out FAQ marker missing")
    item["body"] = item["body"].replace(faq_marker, details + faq_marker, 1)
    for node in item["ld"]:
        if node.get("@type") == "Service":
            node["serviceType"] = "Fit-out and joinery shop drawings"
            node["description"] = "Fit-out and joinery shop drawings for UAE interiors: ceilings, partitions, kitchens, wardrobes and interior elevations, issued as DWG and PDF. Quoted per project."
            node["offers"] = {
                "@type": "Offer",
                "name": "Fit-out and joinery shop drawings",
                "description": "Quote on request. Scope, fee and delivery date are confirmed in writing before work starts.",
                "priceCurrency": "AED",
                "url": "https://d3ddd.com/fitout-shop-drawings/",
            }
        elif node.get("@type") == "FAQPage":
            node["mainEntity"].extend({
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": q,
                "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": a},
            } for q, a in faqs)


def _correct_render_price_claims(item):
    """Pages that denied any published render price. The single still is 650 AED."""
    replacements = {
        "construction-companies-uae/index.html": (
            "There is no published price per image and no published rate per page of a bill.",
            "A single 3D still render is 650 AED, with 50% upfront. Additional views are quoted on request, and there is no published rate per page of a bill.",
        ),
        "real-estate-developers-uae/index.html": (
            "The images are quoted per view or per space after the brief is clear. There is no price per image on this site.",
            "A single 3D still render is 650 AED, with 50% upfront. Additional views, models and walkthroughs are quoted per view or per space after the brief is clear.",
        ),
    }
    pair = replacements.get(item["fn"])
    if not pair or pair[0] not in item["body"]:
        if pair:
            raise SystemExit("price sentence missing on " + item["fn"])
        return
    item["body"] = item["body"].replace(pair[0], pair[1], 1)


def build_landing_pages(g):
    shell = g["shell"]
    out = {}
    for item in _DATA:
        _expand_fitout(item)
        _correct_render_price_claims(item)
        fn = item["fn"]
        P = g["prefix"]("en", fn)
        out[("en", fn)] = shell(
            "en", fn, item["title"], item["desc"], item["body"], item["ld"],
            bilingual=False, preload=item.get("preload"), switch=P + "ar/",
        )
    return out
